WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.800
Good to have you on Tesla's short time, daily, episode 479 from May 21st, 2026.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.540
I'm Patrick coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.260
Here's what you need to know about Tesla today.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:21.340
Xiaomi's YU7 undercuts the Model Y by $4.350 with extra range, raising the stakes for Tesla

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:22.480
in China and beyond.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:28.700
Xiaomi introduced its YU7 crossover at a lower starting price than the Model Y, while

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.340
claiming an additional 50 kilometers of range.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.960
The move directly targets Tesla's best-selling vehicle in a market where price sensitivity

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.940
remains high.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.060
Xiaomi added a lower-price standard variant of its YU7 to the lineup.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.580
The new version widens the price gap with the Model Y and targets buyers who previously

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.580
found the higher trims too expensive.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:56.200
It shows Xiaomi moving quickly to cover more segments of the competitive crossover market.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.340
Chinese competitors are using cost advantages and local supply chains to a road Tesla's

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:02.760
position.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.260
Now moving to software updates in the same market.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.360
Tesla has begun rolling out its supervised, full-self-driving software in China.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:16.820
The expansion aims to improve the appeal of its vehicles amid slowing domestic demand.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.880
Regulators and local infrastructure will determine how quickly the feature gains traction

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:22.480
with buyers.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:28.320
The rollout comes as Tesla works on software differentiation to support sales in that region.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.280
Independent testing of the 10 longest-range electric vehicles showed none of Tesla's

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.920
current models ranking at the top.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:41.120
Real-world results fell short of advertised figures across the board, with several non-Tesla

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.160
models pulling ahead.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.660
The findings add pressure on Tesla's range leadership claims, as competitors release

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:48.600
updated packs.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.380
Several competitors delivered higher real-world distances than their Tesla counterparts under

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.500
identical conditions.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.280
The gap matters because range remains a primary purchase factor for many buyers and directly

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.440
affects Tesla's competitive positioning.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:09.300
Taking a step back from today's headlines, the latest independent range tests reveal

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:14.120
a gap between advertised figures and measured highway performance that challenges the

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.720
long-held view that Tesla simply leads on battery efficiency.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:24.800
The data showed multiple non-Tesla models exceeding Tesla's real-world distances by meaningful

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.640
margins under controlled conditions.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:33.020
This outcome suggests that pack design, thermal management, and aerodynamic execution can

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:37.640
outweigh software advantages once competitors close the initial technology gap.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:43.440
Tesla's vertical integration gives it the ability to iterate on self-format, structural

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.900
battery packs and vehicle aerodynamics in a single loop.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.160
That approach could narrow the measured gap faster than rivals that rely on supplier

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.220
sales and separate chassis programs.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.880
The result is continued pressure to treat range as an engineering target rather than a

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.760
marketing claim if Tesla wants to keep its efficiency reputation intact.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:09.360
Tesla recorded its strongest daily sales pace in Norway so far this quarter.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:14.860
The uptick comes as the company continues to rely on European markets for volume while

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.520
US growth has moderated.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:21.600
Local incentives and model availability appear to be supporting the recent momentum.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.160
Daily Tesla registrations in Norway reach their highest level of the second quarter.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:33.360
The surge suggests European demand can still offset softer US numbers when incentives align.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:40.100
A single buyer took delivery of cyber trucks valued at $131 million in total.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:44.800
Reports indicate Elon Musk is connected to the purchase through one of his companies.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.940
The scale of the order underscores continued internal demand even as broader retail sales

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:51.640
remain modest.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.820
The transaction points to concentrated demand from entities linked to Elon Musk rather

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.500
than broad retail uptake.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.600
It raises questions about how Tesla counts and reports such fleet style orders.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:09.740
Authorities pull the cyber truck from a lake after the owner drove it in deliberately.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:16.160
The incident raises questions about how owners interpret the truck's advertised water-forting capability.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:21.580
Tesla has not commented on whether any software or hardware limits were exceeded.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:26.960
Tesla held a final handover event for the original Model S and Model X.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.120
The gathering focused on the vehicle's role in changing perceptions of electric cars

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.860
rather than new specifications.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:38.460
It marks the end of a production chapter that began more than a decade ago.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:45.660
Before we go, keep an eye on how the new YU7 pricing and the supervised FSD rollout

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.920
play out in China over the coming weeks.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.340
That's your Tesla news for today.

